  "id": "COMPOUND:32420 - PROTEIN:2574",
  "verbalization": "Oblonganoside C is shown to interact with multiple targets that ultimately lead to the cAMP-dependent protein kinase catalytic subunit beta. The evidence suggests that Oblonganoside C may inhibit the cAMP-dependent protein kinase through indirect pathways, as it targets Ent-Gloeosteretriol, which in turn targets the kinase. Similarly, it may also interact with LIM domain kinase 2 and Cytochrome P450 2E1, both of which are known to modulate the activity of cAMP-dependent protein kinase. The scores from the paths indicate a consistent but moderate level of interaction, suggesting a potential role for Oblonganoside C in modulating the kinase activity through these downstream targets. The mechanism is supported by the presence of a well-documented mode of action in the pathways, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the signaling network and underscores the need for further experimental validation to confirm the direct relationship between Oblonganoside C and the cAMP-dependent protein kinase catalytic subunit beta.",
